Testing Set 2: Image Processing

Purpose: To verify that the system correctly receives camera images, comapres them with previous images, and detects changes in the bluffs.

Unit Testing: Test image processing individually to determine whether it correctly compares images. 
Image Processing:
Scenario 1: Two identical images = No changes
Scenario 2: Two images with small differences = Small changes
Scenario 3: Two images with major differences = Major changes

Integration testing: Testing whether the camera continously captures images to transmit to the central site in order for it to get processed for a rating. New images will be constantly compared for any changes within the bluff. The central site also holds a large amount of data so algorithims can be made to predict the movement of the bluffs as well.

System Test: Capture images for it to go into the system to be reviewed for a rating.
Input: System receieves image and determines rating.
Output: System notifies officials of rating.
